Visible tools: list_dir, read_file, read_files, grep, find_references, parallel, codemode, edit, run, shell, knowledge_search, knowledge_read, research_plan, read_tool_result, done, ask_user

Tool contract (use exactly these shapes):
- list_dir: List files in a directory.
  list_dir(args: { "path"?: string })
  {"tool":"list_dir","args":{"path":"."}}

- read_file: Read one file. Large files are returned in complete-line pages. In CodeMode, value is an object: value.text is the page text (a string), with start_line, end_line, total_lines, next_offset and text_complete metadata.
  read_file(args: { "path": string; "offset"?: number /* range 1..* */; "limit"?: number /* range 1..* */ })
  {"tool":"read_file","args":{"path":"app.py"}}
  {"tool":"read_file","args":{"path":"app.py","offset":301,"limit":300}}

- read_files: Read up to 8 files in one step. Do not nest it inside parallel.
  read_files(args: { "paths": Array<string> })
  {"tool":"read_files","args":{"paths":["a.py","b.py"]}}

- grep: Search file contents for literal text before reading when the location is unknown. Uses packaged ripgrep. Defaults to literal, case-insensitive matching; set literal=false for regex, case_sensitive=true for exact case, include for one positive glob, exclude for positive globs to omit, and before_context/after_context for surrounding lines. Use rg braces for alternatives, e.g. include='*.{py,ts}'; comma-separated globs are not alternatives. Globs are relative to the workspace root even when path narrows the search. Exclude directories with an array such as exclude=['src/vendor/**']. Searches hidden and ignored files within the admitted workspace scope, excluding build/VCS directories and symlinks. CodeMode value is a page object with matches and explicit coverage; column_byte is one-based UTF-8 bytes. Read matched files for context.
  grep(args: { "query": string; "path"?: string; "offset"?: number /* range 1..* */; "limit"?: number /* range 1..* */; "literal"?: boolean; "case_sensitive"?: boolean; "include"?: string; "exclude"?: Array<string>; "before_context"?: number /* range 0..* */; "after_context"?: number /* range 0..* */ })
  {"tool":"grep","args":{"query":"login handler","path":"."}}
  {"tool":"grep","args":{"query":"TODO","path":"src","include":"*.{py,ts}","exclude":["src/vendor/**"]}}

- find_references: Find bounded lexical reference hints for a simple symbol. This is not semantic resolution; use read_file before editing.
  find_references(args: { "symbol": string; "path"?: string })
  {"tool":"find_references","args":{"symbol":"createRouter","path":"."}}

